{
  "requirement": "The harness instructs the model to finish by calling\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.agent-harness.submission.mcp`.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The subject `requirements.sdk.graph.agent-harness.submission` has one obligation. The harness must instruct the model to finish by calling `submit_result`. It cites `submission.mcp`, and I treated that as context only. I did not reassess its tool shape or its tests.\n\nThe reviewed tests check this obligation directly:\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tests.rs#fn[assistant_text_and_provider_failure_cannot_become_typed_results]` serializes the first request's `chat_history` and asserts it contains \"Finish by calling submit_result\". This covers the generic `ToolAgent` path.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/configured.rs#mod[tests]/fn[supplied_openai_backend_runs_independent_calls_against_a_local_transport]` captures the real OpenAI-style HTTP request bodies from a local server. For all four requests it asserts the serialized `input` contains \"Finish by calling submit_result\". It runs two independent calls, so it covers both a fresh conversation and a continuation after a tool result.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/configured.rs#mod[tests]/fn[supplied_ollama_backend_delivers_tools_and_results_over_native_chat]` makes the same assertion on the `messages` of both native Ollama chat requests.\n\nThe `submit_result` tool is also checked to be present and to have the expected schema. The tests in `agent/tests.rs` (`default_tool_accepts_scalar_results_and_keeps_the_exact_prefix` and `typed_submission_references_resolve_and_invalid_results_are_agent_errors`) check the tool list and the `result` property. The two backend tests check the same for OpenAI and Ollama. Those checks belong to `submission.mcp`, not to this subject.\n\nThe assertions are real string checks on the request content the model receives. They would fail if the instruction were dropped from the prompt in any of the three backend paths. I found no unaddressed obligation, and there are no acknowledgments.",
